B.Gq=new A.cr("Localization","Figure-of-4 & fencing posture","The extended arm points to the hemisphere opposite it: onset is contralateral. The fencing (M2e) posture also suggests supplementary motor area onset; figure-of-4 is seen in temporal as well as frontal seizures.",B.cU)
B.GD=new A.cr("Localization","Clustered nocturnal seizures","Brief, frequent, clustered nocturnal seizures with rapid recovery point toward a frontal lobe origin.",B.cn)
B.GH=new A.cr("Localization","Elementary visual hallucinations","Brief, colored, circular flashes that start in one hemifield suggest occipital onset; a slowly spreading, mostly black-and-white zigzag (fortification) lasting minutes suggests migraine.",B.cn)
B.GN=new A.cr("Localization","Choking sensation & dysautonomia","Painful unilateral paresthesia with dysautonomia and a choking sensation should raise suspicion for insular onset.",B.cn)
B.GE=new A.cr("Localization","MRI-negative frontal epilepsy","Frontal lobe seizures are frequently MRI-negative even when focal cortical dysplasia is the underlying cause.",B.ev)
B.GJ=new A.cr("Syndromes","Gelastic seizures","Suggest a hypothalamic hamartoma, especially with precocious puberty in a child.",B.cU)
B.Gx=new A.cr("Syndromes","Early-morning myoclonus","Ask every adolescent with early-morning myoclonic jerks about juvenile myoclonic epilepsy before labeling episodes as clumsiness.",B.cU)
B.Gt=new A.cr("Syndromes","Infantile spasms","With developmental regression, a pediatric neurologic emergency requiring urgent EEG (hypsarrhythmia) and treatment.",B.cU)
B.Gy=new A.cr("Syndromes","Catamenial pattern","Best confirmed with a seizure diary correlated against a menstrual calendar, not by history alone.",B.ev)
B.GA=new A.cr("Syndromes","Reflex epilepsy triggers","Photosensitive, reading, musicogenic, hot water and startle epilepsies share a stereotyped trigger-to-seizure relationship \u2014 ask specifically.",B.cn)
B.GI=new A.cr("Mimics","Convulsive syncope","The single most commonly misdiagnosed seizure mimic in adults \u2014 look for a presyncopal prodrome and rapid full recovery.",B.cU)
B.Gw=new A.cr("Mimics","Anoxic myoclonus","Brief myoclonic jerks during a faint do not make an event epileptic.",B.cn)
B.Gz=new A.cr("Mimics","Bedside glucose","Always check during the acute evaluation of any transient event \u2014 hypoglycemia is a readily reversible mimic.",B.ev)
B.GC=new A.cr("Mimics","Migraine aura tempo","Migraine with aura evolves more slowly (minutes) than an epileptic aura (seconds) and is usually followed by headache.",B.cn)
B.GK=new A.cr("Investigations","Normal EEG \u2260 no epilepsy","A single normal interictal EEG does not exclude epilepsy \u2014 sensitivity rises with sleep-deprived and repeated recordings.",B.ev)
B.GB=new A.cr("Investigations","Video-EEG monitoring","Capturing a typical habitual event remains the diagnostic gold standard when the differential is unclear.",B.ev)
